  "challenge": "The line economics are internally coherent as a net credit, not gibberish: WidgetA −5 × $250 and WidgetB +2 × $500 net exactly to the stated total of −$250, and both unit prices match the item catalog exactly (get_item_reference). That pattern is the ordinary shape of a return applied against a small new purchase; AR-005/AR-006 and the AR-002/AR-004 mismatches are then symptoms of filing a credit-memo transaction on an invoice form, not evidence the commercial content is illegitimate. With no prior INV-1009 and an empty vendor name, pure REJECT discards a price-consistent credit that only needs the counterparty identified—so the record is better read as a mis-typed credit memo warranting vendor identification rather than an unpayable nullity.",
  "proposed_outcome": "ESCALATE",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["AR-005", "AR-006", "AR-002", "AR-004", "VN-005"]
